# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bookalyze app (apps/web, app.bookalyze.com): environment variables
#
# Local development: copy this file to apps/web/.env and fill it in.
#   cp apps/web/.env.example apps/web/.env
# The database scripts (pnpm db:setup, db:migrate) read it too. A repo-root .env or .env.local
# still works as well; apps/web/.env wins over it. Local values: docs/SETUP.md → Local development.
# Production / previews: add the names in Vercel → the "bookalyze" project → Settings →
# Environment Variables. Never commit real values.
#
# The public site (bookalyze.com) is a separate Vercel project with its own short list:
# apps/marketing/.env.example.
#
# Each variable is marked:
#   [required]     the app won't start, or a core feature is broken, without it
#   [recommended]  set it in production; something is switched off without it
#   [optional]     has a sensible default, or turns on a feature you may not need yet
#   [never in production]  local development and tests only; leave unset on Vercel
#
# Per-company credentials (Amazon SP-API, Wise, Noon, Walmart, each eBay seller…) do NOT go here.
# They are entered inside the app under each company's Settings → Connections. Only Bookalyze's
# own app keys (Google sign-in, eBay's developer app, Stripe) are set here.
#
# Step-by-step setup for each service: docs/SETUP.md.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. Database (Neon Postgres) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# [required] On Vercel, connect Neon from the project's Storage tab: it sets DATABASE_URL (pooled)
# and DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED (direct) for you, both as the owner role. Nothing else to add.
# The app connects with DATABASE_URL. Tenant queries switch to the app_runtime role inside each
# transaction (withOrg), so row-level security applies even over the owner login.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://neondb_owner:PASSWORD@ep-xxxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/bookalyze?sslmode=require
# [optional] Migrations and seeding use DATABASE_URL_MIGRATOR, else DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED, else
# DATABASE_URL. Use the owner role and Neon's DIRECT (non-pooled) connection string.
DATABASE_URL_MIGRATOR=postgres://neondb_owner:PASSWORD@ep-xxxxx.REGION.aws.neon.tech/bookalyze?sslmode=require
# Set by Neon's Vercel integration (direct connection). Leave unset locally.
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
# GitHub (not Vercel) → repo Settings → Secrets → Actions: DATABASE_URL_MIGRATOR (the same Neon
# owner, direct string) lets the Deploy workflow run safe migrations before Vercel promotes a deploy.

# [never in production] Database tests (pnpm test) use a separate database, so they never touch
# your data. `pnpm db:up` creates it locally.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://bookalyze_app:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/bookalyze_test
TEST_DATABASE_URL_MIGRATOR=postgres://bookalyze_owner:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/bookalyze_test

# ── 2. Sign-in (Better Auth) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [required] Random 32+ character secret. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# Changing it signs everyone out.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# [required] Public URL of the app. http://localhost:3000 locally; https://app.bookalyze.com in
# production. Links in emails and Stripe's return pages are built from it.
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# [recommended] Sign in with Google. Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials →
# Create OAuth client ID (type: Web application). Authorized redirect URIs:
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/google
#   https://app.bookalyze.com/api/auth/callback/google
# Leave empty to hide the Google button.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# [recommended] Preview deployments only: the production URL that handles Google callbacks for
# previews. Set it in Vercel for the Preview environment only: https://app.bookalyze.com
OAUTH_PROXY_PRODUCTION_URL=

# [optional] invite_only (default while private) or open (public launch).
SIGNUP_MODE=invite_only
# [recommended] Comma-separated emails that may always sign up (you, the platform owner). They are
# also the support desk (/admin/support) and get an email for each new ticket and customer reply.
PLATFORM_ADMIN_EMAILS=you@example.com

# ── 3. Email (Resend) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [required] resend.com → API Keys. Verify the bookalyze.com domain under Domains first. Without it
# no email is sent: no sign-up verification, password resets or invitations.
RESEND_API_KEY=
# [optional] Default "Bookalyze <no-reply@bookalyze.com>". Must be on the verified domain.
EMAIL_FROM="Bookalyze <no-reply@bookalyze.com>"
# [recommended] Forwarded invoice requests, receipts by email and replies to support tickets: the
# domain Resend receives for (MX record), and the signing secret of the Resend webhook for
# "email.received" pointing at https://app.bookalyze.com/api/inbound/email.
INBOUND_EMAIL_DOMAIN=
RESEND_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# [never in production] true = write emails to apps/web/.dev-mail.log instead of sending.
EMAIL_DEV_LOG=false

# ── 4. Billing (Stripe) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [optional] Without a key, billing is off and everything stays free. Steps: docs/SETUP.md → Stripe.
# Test mode only: a live key (sk_live_…) is ignored unless STRIPE_LIVE=true.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# [optional] Leave false until you decide billing goes live; only then set true with a live key.
STRIPE_LIVE=false
# [required with a Stripe key] Signing secret (whsec_…) of the webhook pointing at
# https://app.bookalyze.com/api/stripe/webhook, with the events checkout.session.completed,
# customer.subscription.created, customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted,
# invoice.payment_failed and invoice.paid. Plans don't update in the app without it.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# [optional] YYYY-MM-DD. Until this day (and while unset) every company has everything, free.
# After it, each company gets a 30-day free trial of everything, then needs a plan.
BILLING_STARTS_ON=

# ── 5. Support ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [recommended] Shared with the public site (apps/marketing/.env.example): its contact form posts
# enquiries to /api/support/intake with this as a bearer token. 32+ characters:
# openssl rand -hex 32. Set the SAME value in both Vercel projects. Unset: the endpoint is off and
# the site emails instead.
SUPPORT_INTAKE_SECRET=

# ── 6. Public site links ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [optional] Where the shared header and footer on the app's public pages (sign-in, terms,
# privacy) link to. Default https://bookalyze.com.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── 7. Receipts and documents (AWS S3) ────────────────────────────────────────
# [required] Without a bucket, receipts and documents can't be uploaded in production.
# A private bucket with versioning on, CORS allowing PUT from the app's origins, and an IAM user
# limited to that bucket (s3:PutObject, s3:GetObject, s3:DeleteObject). Steps: docs/SETUP.md.
AWS_REGION=ca-central-1
AWS_S3_BUCKET=
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# [never in production as "local"] "s3" (default when AWS_S3_BUCKET is set) or "local" (files in
# apps/web/.uploads; development and CI only). Leave unset on Vercel.
STORAGE_DRIVER=

# ── 8. Scheduled jobs and saved connections ───────────────────────────────────
# [required] Vercel Cron sends this as "Authorization: Bearer …" to /api/cron/* (exchange rates,
# marketplace orders, review requests, listing checks). 16+ characters: openssl rand -base64 32.
# Without it the scheduled jobs refuse to run.
CRON_SECRET=
# [required] Master key that encrypts each company's saved credentials (Wise, Amazon, Noon,
# Walmart, eBay). openssl rand -base64 32. Keep a backup somewhere safe: losing or changing it
# means reconnecting every connection (what was already brought in is unaffected).
APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ── 9. eBay (Bookalyze's own eBay developer app) ──────────────────────────────
# [optional] One app for every company; each company connects its own seller account on eBay's
# page. Without the first three, Connect eBay says it isn't available yet. Steps: docs/SETUP.md → eBay.
# developer.ebay.com → Application Keys: App ID (Client ID) and Cert ID (Client Secret).
EBAY_CLIENT_ID=
EBAY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# User Tokens → the redirect's RuName (not a URL). Its accepted and declined URLs are
# https://app.bookalyze.com/api/ebay/callback; its privacy policy URL is
# https://app.bookalyze.com/privacy-policy
EBAY_RU_NAME=
# Alerts & Notifications → Marketplace account deletion: a token you make up (32–80 letters,
# digits, _ or -), entered there too. Endpoint: https://app.bookalyze.com/api/ebay/account-deletion
EBAY_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=
# Leave unset for live keys (production). Set to sandbox only with Sandbox keys.
# EBAY_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# ── Test stand-ins ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# [never in production] Leave unset: the real APIs. End-to-end tests point them at local stand-ins
# in apps/web/e2e/.
# WISE_API_URL=
# AMAZON_LWA_URL=
# AMAZON_SPAPI_URL=
# NOON_API_URL=
# WALMART_API_URL=
# EBAY_AUTH_URL=
# EBAY_API_URL=
# EBAY_APIZ_URL=
# STRIPE_API_URL=
